    <node id="failure_6bde3f2c39b8_algorithm_random_forest__llm_proposed_v2">
      <data key="d0">FailureExperience</data>
      <data key="d5">failure_6bde3f2c39b8_algorithm_random_forest__llm_proposed_v2</data>
      <data key="d56">failure</data>
      <data key="d8">algorithm_random_forest</data>
      <data key="d45">6bde3f2c39b8:algorithm_random_forest__llm_proposed:v2</data>
      <data key="d17">binary_classification</data>
      <data key="d40">customer analytics</data>
      <data key="d51">tabular</data>
      <data key="d41">churn</data>
      <data key="d57">runtime_failure</data>
      <data key="d58">The error occurred because the Random Forest classifier attempted to fit the model on a dataset containing non-numeric categorical variables without proper encoding. Specifically, the 'region' column, which contains string values like 'east', was not appropriately transformed into a numerical format before fitting the model.</data>
      <data key="d59">The triggering condition was the presence of unencoded categorical data in the training dataset, leading to a ValueError when the model tried to fit the data.</data>
      <data key="d60">To address this issue, the preprocessing step should include encoding categorical variables into numerical form using OneHotEncoder instead of 'passthrough'. This ensures all categorical features are properly converted to numerical format before being fed into the Random Forest model.</data>
      <data key="d61">False</data>
      <data key="d62">When working with machine learning models that require numerical input, ensure all categorical features are properly encoded into numerical formats before training the model.</data>
      <data key="d15">2026-09-07T16:16:38.646501+00:00</data>
    </node>
    <node id="failure_6bde3f2c39b8_algorithm_random_forest__llm_proposed_v3">
      <data key="d0">FailureExperience</data>
      <data key="d5">failure_6bde3f2c39b8_algorithm_random_forest__llm_proposed_v3</data>
      <data key="d56">failure</data>
      <data key="d8">algorithm_random_forest</data>
