      <data key="d17">binary_classification</data>
      <data key="d40">customer analytics</data>
      <data key="d51">tabular</data>
      <data key="d41">churn</data>
      <data key="d57">runtime_failure</data>
      <data key="d58">RandomForestClassifier does not accept missing values encoded as NaN natively.</data>
      <data key="d59">Input data contained NaN values which were not handled appropriately by the preprocessing steps.</data>
      <data key="d60">Add an imputation step to the preprocessing pipeline to handle missing values before they reach the classifier. Use SimpleImputer for numerical features and MostFrequentImputer for categorical features.</data>
      <data key="d61">False</data>
      <data key="d62">Ensure that any machine learning algorithm used cannot handle missing values natively, and include appropriate preprocessing steps to manage these values.</data>
      <data key="d15">2026-09-07T16:16:43.361549+00:00</data>
    </node>
